 "about": [
  "The scenery kit library (Ride Anywhere v2, phase D: interfaces/scenery.md). Each kind the features baker keeps (tools/feature_bake.py KINDS) has a row: the phase D round that models it, and its 'default' (every region) with any of the thirteen regional kits' ids (data/region_kits.json) under 'regions' laid over it.",
  "A row's fields: model ('SCRIPT:MODEL', drawn by scripts/scenery/SCRIPT.gd: 'standin:post' is round 0's post, until the round's thread adds its own), reach (m: drawn while the camera is this close), and whatever else the round's model reads. Nothing here decides where a thing is: that is the map's (features.json).",
  "A kit row may also say 'sea': true (the model may stand offshore: unknown ground counts as sea level). A reach past SceneryStreamer.REACH (2000 m) has its blocks laid out that far (FAR_MOST, 8000 m, at most)."
 ],
